---
description: Prefer trash-cli for deleting user files
alwaysApply: true
---

Prefer `trash-put` over `rm` when deleting user files.

- Use `trash-put PATH` for files under `$HOME` and other user data.
- Do not use `rm -rf` on home directories, documents, or project source unless the user asked for a permanent delete.
- `rm` is OK for build/cache/tmp paths (`node_modules`, `dist`, `/tmp`, `/var/tmp`) and when the user asked to destroy a file.
- If unsure, use `trash-put` and say the file went to trash.
